  "text": "The name Cai marks an early Irish hero. Some name him the first brehon, or judge, of Ireland. He belonged to the people called the Milesians. Cai studied in Egypt. There he learned the law of Moses. He arranged the marriage of the leader Mil to the princess Scota. Scota was the daughter of the Pharaoh. When the giant flood came, Cai sailed with Moses. Later he rejoined his own people in central Europe. From there he sailed to Ireland and served as judge to the settlers. The Arthurian hero Kay also bears this name.",
